(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Classes (PY5c; CPython's Objects/typeobject.c and builtin___build_class__ of Python/bltinmodule.c):"] [9 1 "// the class statement's __build_class__, type.__new__ with its C3 MRO, metaclasses, __prepare__,"] [10 1 "// __mro_entries__, __init_subclass__ and __set_name__, the instances of classes, object.__new__ and"] [11 1 "// object.__init__, and the slots of a class filled from its special methods (fixup_slot_dispatchers)."] [13 1 "// Instance is an instance of a class (a heap type): its class, its __dict__ (nil under __slots__"] [14 1 "// without __dict__), its __slots__' values, and, for a class deriving from a built-in type other than"] [15 1 "// object, BaseException and type, the built-in base's value the inherited slots work on."] [25 1 "// classInfo is what type.__new__ records of a class beyond the Type (CPython's heap type fields)."] [27 21 "// this class's own __slots__ (mangled), in order"] [28 21 "// the instance's slot count, the bases' included"] [29 21 "// its instances have a __dict__"] [30 21 "// the built-in solid base: object, BaseException, type, or another built-in"] [31 21 "// __abstractmethods__ non-empty"] [48 1 "// builtinSolid is the built-in type whose instance layout t's instances have (solid_base without the"] [49 1 "// heap types' __slots__)."] [70 1 "// solidBase is solid_base: the most derived type adding to the instance layout."] [83 1 "// unwrap is the built-in value of an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type, else o."] [91 1 "// ---- __build_class__ ----"] [94 2 "// PY5b's hooks (§7.1): the core accessors take a subclass's built-in value; a bound method of a Python"] [95 2 "// function is called by pushing its frame"] [127 1 "// dictArgs are a keyword dictionary as a call's trailing keyword arguments."] [214 20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [245 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [286 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [303 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [385 2 "// __module__, __qualname__, __doc__"] [405 32 "// not when __slots__ names __doc__ (typing's _SpecialForm): the slot's descriptor is it"] [407 2 "// __new__ a staticmethod, __init_subclass__ and __class_getitem__ classmethods"] [416 2 "// __slots__"] [420 20 "// a class without __slots__ gives its instances a __dict__"] [481 2 "// __classcell__, __classdictcell__"] [498 2 "// __eq__ without __hash__ makes the class unhashable"] [506 2 "// __set_name__"] [518 2 "// __init_subclass__"] [533 1 "// checkLayouts refuses bases whose instance layouts conflict."] [544 1 "// bestBase is best_base: the base whose solid base is the most derived."] [562 1 "// c3MRO is the C3 linearization of t over its bases (mro_internal's mro_implementation)."] [621 1 "// mangle is _Py_Mangle: __x in class C is _C__x."] [644 1 "// ---- object.__new__, object.__init__ ----"] [646 1 "// overrides is a heap class of t's MRO defining name, or, for __new__, t's built-in solid base not"] [647 1 "// object (a built-in type's inherited slot cannot be told from its own: Go's functions do not compare)."] [716 2 "// The data model's slots of object and type (REQUEST to PY5b: leave these to class.go)."] [729 1 "// ---- the slots of a class (fixup_slot_dispatchers, update_slot) ----"] [735 1 "// pyDefined is name defined by a heap class of t's MRO (a Python method), and its value."] [744 1 "// fixupSlots fills t's slots: the built-in solid base's (unwrapping a built-in subclass's value),"] [745 1 "// then a dispatcher for each special method a class of the MRO defines. Rerun on a class's"] [746 1 "// special attribute's assignment, for it and its subclasses."] [767 4 "// dict's subscript sees the subclass's instance (its __missing__; dict's accessors take the"] [768 4 "// instance through BuiltinValueHook): PY5e, part 2b"] [1052 1 "// unwrapSlots makes a built-in base's slots work on its subclass's instances: each argument that is"] [1053 1 "// such an instance replaced by its value, and the base's __new__'s value wrapped in the instance."] [1121 1 "// wrapNew is a built-in __new__ called for a class deriving from it: its value in an instance."] [1138 1 "// callSpecial calls o's special method name (looked up on its type, as CPython's lookup_maybe_method)."] [1147 1 "// callSpecialOr is callSpecial, NotImplemented when o's type has no such method."] [1156 1 "// CallSpecial calls o's special method name, found reports whether o's type has it (for the"] [1157 1 "// built-ins with no slot: __abs__, __divmod__, __round__, __format__, __reversed__ ...)."] [1167 1 "// asIndex is operator.index(o)."] [1190 1 "// objectRichCompare is object's __eq__ (identity), __ne__ (__eq__ inverted), the rest NotImplemented."] [1216 1 "// updateSubclassSlots refills the slots of t and its subclasses after a special attribute changed"] [1217 1 "// (update_slot over the subclasses: the type version tags' invalidation)."] [1228 1 "// IsSubclass is issubclass(c, cls) with __subclasscheck__; IsInstanceOf isinstance(o, cls) with"] [1229 1 "// __instancecheck__ (PyObject_IsInstance, PyObject_IsSubclass)."] [1343 1 "// posArgs checks a built-in's positional argument count, CPython's messages."] [1361 1 "// ---- object's pickling protocol (typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex__, reduce_newobj, object_getstate) ----"] [1363 1 "// importModule is __import__(name) through the interpreter's builtins (PY5e's import system)."] [1372 1 "// importErrorType is ImportError when the runtime has it, else RuntimeError."] [1388 1 "// objectGetState is object.__getstate__: the instance's __dict__ (None when empty), with its"] [1389 1 "// __slots__' values as a second dictionary."] [1507 1 "// BuiltinValue is the built-in value an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type carries"] [1508 1 "// (a list subclass's list), else o itself: for the core types' functions taking their subclasses."] [1511 1 "// slotsName is __slots__ (a str or an iterable of them) in the class namespace naming name (PY6a)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[42 24] [73 25] [85 27] [98 26] [99 35] [120 32] [166 33] [195 32] [222 60] [231 26] [232 30] [250 24] [330 24] [346 48] [375 50] [382 33] [387 32] [388 40] [393 46] [396 37] [408 48] [412 41] [421 35] [423 24] [478 34] [482 38] [490 42] [508 76] [514 61] [526 33] [649 32] [669 61] [671 29] [677 26] [772 55] [773 38] [779 38] [855 55] [863 51] [878 38] [894 38] [916 31] [934 38] [947 42] [980 32] [992 32] [1055 16] [1058 15] [1061 16] [1064 16] [1067 15] [1070 23] [1073 16] [1076 16] [1079 19] [1082 19] [1085 20] [1089 22] [1092 23] [1095 23] [1100 21] [1104 17] [1107 15] [1110 17] [1113 15] [1116 16] [1169 22] [1172 30] [1177 31] [1231 25] [1234 28] [1243 60] [1254 25] [1258 47] [1259 26] [1265 33] [1276 28] [1285 60] [1297 31] [1300 33] [1335 43] [1374 75] [1392 25] [1395 30] [1399 45] [1414 57] [1431 61] [1451 33] [1460 37] [1482 48] [1489 23] [1517 23] [1525 23]]} (go/file "class.go" :imports [


